      "claim": "Schisandrin B reached detectable and substantial mouse brain tissue concentrations after systemic administration, with a maximum of 0.327 µg/g at 2 h, supporting meaningful CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "high",
  "decision_summary": "All retrieved structurally related molecules show direct experimental evidence of BBB penetration after systemic administration, including brain tissue detection, CSF detection, and brain/plasma equilibration. This consistent positive evidence supports meaningful CNS access for the query molecule.",
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct experimental record for the query molecule itself; evidence is based on structurally similar analogs.",
    "All CNS access data come from normal rodents rather than brain tumor or glioma models, though the tumor condition would not be expected to reduce systemic CNS access."
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [],
  "revision_action": "initial"
}

